  "worked_solution": "We are given the unit rate of $$0.08$ per foot (dollars per foot). To find the amount of copper wire that Anne can buy for $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in feet per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n0.08\\,\\text{dollars per foot}\\,\\to \\,1÷0.08=12.5\\,\\text{feet per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $12.5$ feet per dollar. Therefore, Anne can buy $12.5$ feet of copper wire.",
